// f_ink -- edge pooling (spec FR-007, reversed 2026-11-09; plan ADR-8, T035). Mirror: tests/modules/ink/ink_mirror.pool.
// rim = clamp(2 * max(S - Bp, 0) / max(S, 0.001), 0, 1); P = S * ((1 - edge_pool) + edge_pool * rim).
// The rim stays at the value of the mark and the body thins. The earlier form raised the rim instead, and above 1 a screen clips
// it, so it could not show on a full-value mark. Dividing by S gives a partial tone the same rim, in proportion.
// First input: Bp, the blur of S at pool_width. Second input: S. The blur arrives last and jit.gl.pix renders on its
// left inlet, so the blur has to be the left one, or this stage would use last frame's rim.
pool_c(sc, bc, amt) {
    rim = clamp(2.0 * max(sc - bc, 0.0) / max(sc, 0.001), 0.0, 1.0);
    return sc * ((1.0 - amt) + amt * rim);
}

Param edge_pool(0.0);

out1 = vec(pool_c(nearest(in2, norm).x, nearest(in1, norm).x, edge_pool), pool_c(nearest(in2, norm).y, nearest(in1, norm).y, edge_pool), pool_c(nearest(in2, norm).z, nearest(in1, norm).z, edge_pool), 1.0);
